2026-10-23T09:00:12.8716537Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8716874Z 
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8716996Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8717237Z 
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8717426Z Commands:
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8717833Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8718526Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8719413Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8720183Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8720976Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8721637Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8722246Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8722948Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8723595Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8724180Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8724701Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8725554Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8726135Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8726555Z   help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8726893Z 
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8726993Z Options:
2026-10-23T09:00:12.8727349Z       --json               Emit machine-readable JSON to stdout; logs remain on stderr
